1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,143
Quick recap before we wrap.

2
00:00:02,143 --> 00:00:06,429
The five core principles — clarity, context, structure, constraints, examples.

3
00:00:06,429 --> 00:00:07,714
They're the foundation.

4
00:00:07,714 --> 00:00:10,714
Every technique we covered builds on them.

5
00:00:10,714 --> 00:00:15,429
The eight techniques — zero-shot, few-shot, chain-of-thought, role prompting, iterative refinement,

6
00:00:15,429 --> 00:00:17,143
template, negative prompting, comparative.

7
00:00:17,143 --> 00:00:20,571
Each one fits a specific kind of task.

8
00:00:20,571 --> 00:00:24,857
Pick the right one, and your prompts get noticeably better.

9
00:00:24,857 --> 00:00:29,143
The four advanced patterns — system prompts, temperature, prompt chaining,

10
00:00:29,143 --> 00:00:30,343
meta prompting.

11
00:00:30,343 --> 00:00:33,771
These are how production work gets done —

12
00:00:33,771 --> 00:00:38,486
when you've moved past one-off questions and you're building real workflows.

13
00:00:38,486 --> 00:00:42,343
And the practice loop — write, test, iterate, document.

14
00:00:42,343 --> 00:00:44,486
The skill isn't memorizing techniques.

15
00:00:44,486 --> 00:00:47,914
It's noticing when a prompt isn't quite right,

16
00:00:47,914 --> 00:00:50,486
and knowing how to fix it.

17
00:00:50,486 --> 00:00:54,771
Three things to do before you call this course complete.

18
00:00:54,771 --> 00:00:56,914
First — take the quiz.

19
00:00:56,914 --> 00:00:59,914
It's in the course folder, called quiz.md.

20
00:00:59,914 --> 00:01:02,914
Twelve questions, ten minutes, answer key included.

21
00:01:02,914 --> 00:01:04,200
Score yourself honestly.

22
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:07,629
Nine out of twelve is the pass mark.

23
00:01:07,629 --> 00:01:10,629
If you fall short on a section,

24
00:01:10,629 --> 00:01:14,057
re-watch the corresponding video and try again —

25
00:01:14,057 --> 00:01:17,914
it's not a graded exam, it's a calibration check.

26
00:01:17,914 --> 00:01:20,914
Second — work through the learner workbook.

27
00:01:20,914 --> 00:01:25,200
Four practice tasks, each takes about ten to fifteen minutes.

28
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:28,200
The first is an internal email —

29
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:32,057
a perfect first run at applying all five principles.

30
00:01:32,057 --> 00:01:35,057
The second is a few-shot triage exercise.

31
00:01:35,057 --> 00:01:38,057
The third is a chain-of-thought decision problem.

32
00:01:38,057 --> 00:01:41,914
The fourth is iterative refinement on a creative brief.

33
00:01:41,914 --> 00:01:46,629
Each task ends with a rubric you can check yourself against.

34
00:01:46,629 --> 00:01:47,914
When you're done,

35
00:01:47,914 --> 00:01:51,771
you'll have something I want you to keep —

36
00:01:51,771 --> 00:01:53,486
a starter prompt library.

37
00:01:53,486 --> 00:01:57,343
Four prompts you actually wrote, that solve real problems,

38
00:01:57,343 --> 00:02:00,343
that you can keep tweaking and reusing.

39
00:02:00,343 --> 00:02:03,771
That library is the artifact of this course.

40
00:02:03,771 --> 00:02:06,343
It's worth more than any certificate.

41
00:02:06,343 --> 00:02:11,057
Third — when you're ready, the next course is AI Agents.

42
00:02:11,057 --> 00:02:15,771
That's where we take everything you just learned and use it

43
00:02:15,771 --> 00:02:20,057
to build systems that don't just respond to prompts —

44
00:02:20,057 --> 00:02:24,343
they plan, they take actions, and they run real workflows.

45
00:02:24,343 --> 00:02:26,486
Prompt engineering is the foundation.

46
00:02:26,486 --> 00:02:29,486
Agents are what you build on top.

47
00:02:29,486 --> 00:02:30,771
One last thing.

48
00:02:30,771 --> 00:02:35,057
The skill you've started building today only deepens with practice.

49
00:02:35,057 --> 00:02:39,771
Every prompt you write from here on is a chance to

50
00:02:39,771 --> 00:02:42,343
use one of these techniques deliberately.

51
00:02:42,343 --> 00:02:44,914
Notice when you reach for chain-of-thought.

52
00:02:44,914 --> 00:02:48,771
Notice when few-shot would have saved you a back-and-forth.

53
00:02:48,771 --> 00:02:53,486
The point of the workbook isn't to pass a test —

54
00:02:53,486 --> 00:02:55,629
it's to build the muscle.

55
00:02:55,629 --> 00:02:56,914
Thanks for watching.

56
00:02:56,914 --> 00:02:59,486
Now go write some prompts. ---
